-- title:
--   Hopf quotient system cutting out a saturated Galois-stable submodule
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p/\mathbb Q_p$ with $K$ finite over $\mathbb Q_p$, and write $\mathcal O =$ [`PadicAlgCl.ringOfIntegers p K`](def/PadicAlgCl_RingOfIntegers.html#L11) for the intersection of the integral closure of $\mathbb Z_p$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ with $K$. Let $G$ be a [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199) over $\mathcal O$ with parameters $p, h$: commutative, cocommutative, finite free Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebras `G.level v` of rank $p^{vh}$, with surjective bialgebra transitions `G.transition v : G.level (v+1) → G.level v` whose kernels are the ideals generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$. Let $M$ be a $\mathbb Z_p$-submodule of the Tate module $T$ of the point group $G.\mathrm{Points}(\overline{\mathbb Q}_p)$ — sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$ — assumed stable under the coordinatewise action of every $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$, and saturated: $r\ne 0$ in $\mathbb Z_p$ and $r\cdot x\in M$ force $x\in M$. The assertion is the existence of commutative rings $B_v$, each a cocommutative finite free Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with surjective bialgebra maps $\pi_v : G.\mathrm{level}\,v \to B_v$ and $t_v : B_{v+1}\to B_v$ such that `G.transition v` followed by $\pi_v$ equals $\pi_{v+1}$ followed by $t_v$, and such that for every $v$ and every point $g\in G.\mathrm{Point}(\overline{\mathbb Q}_p)\,v$ (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $G.\mathrm{level}\,v\to\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ in the convolution group) the underlying algebra map of $g$ factors as $\pi_v$ followed by some $\mathcal O$-algebra map $B_v\to\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ if and only if the image of $g$ under `G.pointsMkAdd` at level $v$ is the $v$-th component of some element of $M$.
--
--   This is the integral form of the first step of Tate's Proposition 12 in the theory of $p$-divisible groups: the schematic closures over $\mathcal O$ of the finite subgroups of the generic fibres cut out by a Galois-stable saturated $\mathbb Z_p$-submodule $M$ of the Tate module, presented on the Hopf-algebra side as a compatible system of finite free quotients $\pi_v$ whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$-points are exactly the level-$v$ components of $M$. It is used to produce the $p$-divisible subgroup attached to $M$ and the uniqueness of the accompanying family of bialgebra maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_exists_hopf_quotient_system_points_iff_mem_of_forall_smul_mem_of_ringOfIntegers.lean

